			},
			"date": "2024-08-06T21:30:03.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> There are so many ways to do things in AWS! If you eventually want a friendlier first-party package/deploy story that isn't the result of clicking around the console, check out SAM. Also not sure how many requests per month are hitting it, but you could eliminate API GW in favor of a Lambda function URL and save those costs. Come on in, the water's fine!<br><a href=\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/serverless-application-model/latest/developerguide/serverless-getting-started-hello-world.html\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">docs.aws.amazon.com/serverless</span><span class=\"invisible\">-application-model/latest/developerguide/serverless-getting-started-hello-world.html</span></a> <br><a href=\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/urls-configuration.html\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/lat</span><span class=\"invisible\">est/dg/urls-configuration.html</span></a></p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
