			"date": "2024-08-07T18:44:07.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://bensie.social/@james\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>james</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> I'd also recommend SAM CLI for deploying lambda functions. It is relatively easy to use and you can take the reigns in your hand with a Makefile. I'd still recommend API Gateway if you want to implement your own authorization mechanism which you can deploy in another lambda and configure it for your API Gateway resources. Makes it convenient to put OIDC introspection in front of multiple REST endpoints.</p>",
